Description: On-screen keyboard (DECKSMITHOS_TOUCH_KEYBOARD)
 With DECKSMITHOS_TOUCH_KEYBOARD set, an on-screen keyboard appears at the
 bottom of the window while a text field has the focus: the library search
 box (its own keyboard: SEARCH = Return, CLEAR clears the search) and any
 other editable QLineEdit (an application event filter: preferences,
 renaming, table cell editors; ENTER = Return), not spin boxes. Digits,
 letters, - and ', Backspace (repeats while held), CLEAR, SPACE, HIDE; 45 %
 of the window height. Its keys never take the focus; they send key events
 to the field. Styled with WTouchKeyboard and #TouchKeyboardKey. Mixxx has
 no on-screen keyboard on Linux (only iOS's system keyboard). Without the
 variable nothing changes.
Author: DecksmithOS
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-22
